# Api\Data field constants

When reading or writing entity field keys in PHP arrays (DataProviders, Save controllers, repositories, listings, etc.), **always** use constants from the matching `Api\Data\*Interface` — never hardcode strings like `'use_config_rounding_precision'`, `'method_id'`, `'is_active'`.

```php
// ❌
$data['use_config_rounding_precision'] = '1';
$data['is_active'] = 1;

// ✅
use Aheadworks\ShippingTableRates\Api\Data\ShippingMethodInterface;

$data[ShippingMethodInterface::USE_CONFIG_ROUNDING_PRECISION] = '1';
$data[ShippingMethodInterface::IS_ACTIVE] = 1;
```

Do not invent parallel string keys. If a constant is missing on the interface, add it there first.
